HWf","user":{"login":"Watersilver","id":35609105,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NjA5MTA1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35609105?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Watersilver","html_url":"https://github.com/Watersilver","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Watersilver/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Watersilver/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Watersilver/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Watersilver/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Watersilver/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Watersilver/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Watersilver/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Watersilver/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Watersilver/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-05T08:38:22Z","updated_at":"2025-04-05T08:38:22Z","body":"Still an issue in v4.4.1.\n\nAnyone found a workaround?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2780591519/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790582020","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100955#issuecomment-2790582020","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100955","id":2790582020,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mVOcE","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-09T18:25:08Z","updated_at":"2025-04-09T18:25:08Z","body":"> Anyone found a workaround?\n\n@Watersilver I'm using one but it's a very complex solution.\nI made custom GDScript classes + JS class to handle audio from the web side, and I'm loading the audio dynamically (to also benefit from async fetching and reduced startup downloads) through JS using Web Audio API. Web uses separate files and `fetch`, while other platforms include them in the PCK and do it the Godot way.\n\nIf you want a simpler GDScript-only solution to fix just this, you might have to make a custom wrapper class that plays looping audio with looping disabled and manually replays it every time from the proper starting point, assuming that works.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790582020/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4850009717","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100955#issuecomment-4850009717","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100955","id":4850009717,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIRVGdQ","user":{"login":"tarnishedmoth","id":87274781,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3Mjc0Nzgx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87274781?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tarnishedmoth","html_url":"https://github.com/tarnishedmoth","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tarnishedmoth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tarnishedmoth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tarnishedmoth/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tarnishedmoth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tarnishedmoth/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tarnishedmoth/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tarnishedmoth/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tarnishedmoth/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tarnishedmoth/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-01T03:33:08Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T04:03:34Z","body":"Just wanted to chime in and say I'm encountering this issue too. I have an OGG file that loops with an offset about 8 seconds in. When playing the web export, no matter the import configuration or the audio player configuration, it always loops from the very beginning, ignoring the offset. I have not tested to see if this is specific to OGG or not.\n\nAs a workaround I disabled the built-in Loop properties and hooked the `AudioStreamPlayer.finished` signal to `play()` again from the time position, although this introduces a slight hiccup it's a lot better than the wrong behavior. I haven't investigated, but it might be possible to reduce the hiccup by tracking the position yourself rather than relying on the signal...","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4850009717/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]